{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-24T20:46:02.613Z","data":{"text":"Done. The task verify and the proposal verify both pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `fixes` end-to-end for task 1 of change 074:\n\n- **`src/core/spec/parser.ts`** — `SpecData.fixes`, parsed through a new `normalizeChangeIds` helper shared with `depends_on` (numeric ids pad to 3 digits, absent/non-array → `[]`).\n- **`src/core/spec/linter.ts`** — reports `fixes names missing change: <id>` for each missing `fixes` target.\n- **`src/core/status/queue-parser.ts`** — `QueueItem.fixes` plus a `parseFixesLine` helper for the optional `Fixes:` line after `Depends on:`; rejects empty, invalid, repeated, self, forward/unknown, and duplicate lines with queue path + item context, excludes the line from the body, and keeps the raw-section hash semantics.\n- **`src/core/status/queue-state.ts`** — unlanded `fixes` appended to `unmetDependencies` after unlanded dependencies.\n- **`src/core/status/queue-planning.ts`** — `QueuePlanSelection.landedFixes`, resolved by a shared `resolveLanded`.\n- **`src/cli/plan-queue.ts` / `src/core/foundation/new.ts`** — `createQueueChange` → `createChange` → `createNewSpec` → `seedProposal` writes `fixes: [\"<id>\"]` on the line after `depends_on` only when non-empty.\n- **`tests/fixes-declaration.test.ts`** — new suite covering parsing normalization, the lint error, every invalid `Fixes:` case, the waiting rule, and `osq plan --next --print`.\n\nNote: `src/core/foundation/new.ts` needed its expanded `createNewSpec` options compressed (shared `IdList` alias) to stay within the 250-line source budget.\n\nTouched: src/cli/plan-queue.ts, src/core/foundation/new.ts, src/core/spec/linter.ts, src/core/spec/parser.ts, src/core/status/queue-parser.ts, src/core/status/queue-planning.ts, src/core/status/queue-state.ts, tests/fixes-declaration.test.ts"}}
